  "worked_solution": "First, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant. \n\nMaking a substitution $xy=u,$ $\\text{d}y=\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}u,$ we get.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{1}x{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{0}^{x}\\frac{1}{x}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{0}^{x}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{e}^{u}]_{0}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}-1)\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{x}-1)\\,\\text{d}x & =[{e}^{x}-x]_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(e-1)-(1-0) \\\\  & =e-2\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
